				//! <Function Comment="Method CoupleGearPolynom couples a slave axis to a master axis by inclusion of a gear factor using polynomials in different ways:&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;1) use a polynom of 5th degree&#13;&#10;2) couple a polynom of 3rd degree and one of 5th degree&#13;&#10;3) couple a polynom of 4th degree with a linear polynom and a polynom of 4th degree&#13;&#10;4) couple a polynom of 3rd degree with a polynom of 4th degree and a linear polynom with a polynom of 4th degree&#13;&#10;5) couple a polynom of 2nd degree with a linear polynom and a polynom of 2nd degree&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;the following conditions for the slave are always checked&#13;&#10;a) for the velocity V: 0 &lt;= V &lt;= maximal velocity&#13;&#10;b) for the acceleration/deceleration A: maximal deceleration &lt;= A &lt;= maximal acceleration&#13;&#10;c) for the jerk J in the cases 1), 2), 3) an 4): -maximal jerk &lt;= J &lt;= maximal jerk" Name="CoupleGearPolynom_v"/>
